# intro
rep(r"Measured against the formation standard \cref{inh:recursive-formation}, the main theorem establishes selection, exact inheritance, and compression on an open class over a finite window. It does not establish interaction necessity (F5): in the regime of its proof, integrations indicate that the null flow of \cref{inh:null-flow} produces the same membership history (\cref{open:null-control}). Every block relation is transient, and the selector later merges the exterior pair (\cref{open:final-merge}). The construction is therefore a two-stage selection with exact inheritance, not a recursive formation.",
    r"The compression group is a gauge group of the population in the sense of \cref{ch:foundations}; within this construction the gauge structure supplies the orbits that a parent forgets and does no dynamical work. Measured against the formation standard \cref{inh:recursive-formation}, the main theorem establishes selection, exact inheritance, and compression on an open class over a finite window. It establishes neither interaction necessity (F5) nor the counterfactual clause (F6b). In the regime of its proof, integrations of the limit field indicate that the nulls of \cref{inh:null-flow} form the same blocks in the same stages (\cref{open:null-control}); this is not proved. Every block relation is transient, and the selector later merges the exterior pair (\cref{open:final-merge}). The construction is therefore not shown to be a recursive formation, and it is not shown to be a two-stage selection with exact inheritance either, since no clause is shown to fail.")

